<title>USA: Pioneer-Standard to offer 3 mln shrs.</title>
<headline>Pioneer-Standard to offer 3 mln shrs.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pioneer-Standard Electronics Inc said Friday it plans a public offering of 3.0 million shares at $13 each.</p>
<p>The company said it would use proceeds to pay down debt.</p>
<p>It said it granted the underwriters an option to buy up to an additional 450,000 shares to cover over-allotments.</p>
<p>The underwriters are Lazard Freres &amp; Co, Cleary Gull Reiland &amp; McDevitt, and McDonald &amp; Co Securities, Pioneer-Standard said.</p>
<p>The company distributes industrial electronic components and computer systems products.</p>
